{"id": "128650", "revid": "2441334", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=128650", "title": "Farmingdale (New York)", "text": "Farmingdale is a village in New York. Officially, it is part of Oyster Bay, but this town with just over 8,000 inhabitants is a place of its own.\nGet in.\nBy train.\n is a station on the Ronkonkoma Line of the Long Island Rail Road, which connects Ronkonkoma with New York City.\nBy car.\nThe main roads in and out of here are the New York State routes 24 (Conklin Street), 109 (Fulton Street), and 110 (Broad Hollow Road).\nBy bus.\nNassau Inter-County Express operates a number of bus connections to Farmingdale.\nBy plane.\nThe nearest airport is Republic Airport, which is literally just a few miles east of the village.\nEat.\nThere's a fairly good choice when it comes to picking a place to eat. Most of the restaurants are on or just off Main Street."}
